            <ArticleTitle>[Laparoscopic colon resection in carcinoma--beneficial or not?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>577-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It was the aim of our study to investigate the role of laparoscopic colorectal cancer resection for cure. Postoperative morbidity, pain and hospital stay (n = 21) was reduced and patients' recovery accelerated compared to conventionally operated patients (n = 54). The number of resected lymph nodes and tumor distances were comparable; however, portal recurrences remain the main problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
